WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.749
A cleaned value should be explainable In these
examples we remove

00:00:05.762 --> 00:00:11.402
formatting noise and apply a documented abbreviation
rule We are not

00:00:11.415 --> 00:00:17.031
inventing new information Keeping raw and cleaned
values side by side

00:00:17.044 --> 00:00:22.799
is useful during development because it makes every
transformation visible That

00:00:22.826 --> 00:00:26.128
helps catch over-cleaning and makes the process
easier to audit
